- Story & Context: In the wet autumn of 2018, engineer-turned-MC Sora Vance spliced a live cello feed directly into the Boulevard Saint-Laurent toll gantries, broadcasting over the municipal frequency during rush hour to paralyze traffic with sound. The wet asphalt vibrated with low-end sub-bass while drivers turned off their engines to hear Maya Lin’s cello weeping through the roadside emergency speakers. Local police scrambled to trace the signal, but could only find a loop pedal locked inside a utility box dripping with condensation. Sora watched from a diner booth across the street, whispering into a portable cassette recorder: "We mapped the avenue using only what they silenced."
