Track 3: Did the Intersection Speak to You?
- Story & Context: Legend says this track was never formally mixed, but compiled from ninety separate pirate radio bootlegs recorded by listeners during the citywide transit blackout of 2021. The recording captures the exact moment the collective hijacked thirty pedestrian crossing signals at once, transforming their clicking audio-cues into a rhythmic swing pattern across forty city blocks. Commuters gathered in the middle of dead intersections, dancing in silence around small portable speakers playing Lin's majestic, soaring cello lines. The line "Leave your ticket in the drain, we own the track now" became a graffiti tag sprayed across every metro station in the city by morning.
